WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.497
Warning! Warning!

2
00:00:01.497 --> 00:00:06.705
I built this with AI and text to speech, because I can't narrate for shit!

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:12.839
Hey, Dreamer here, and welcome to season two, where we make the world play.

4
00:00:12.839 --> 00:00:17.957
First up, items: the gear, the money, and the settings that hold it all together.

5
00:00:19.367 --> 00:00:21.436
Open Items, then Premade Items.

6
00:00:21.436 --> 00:00:24.574
We've got throwing knives, a patched ring coat,

7
00:00:24.574 --> 00:00:28.312
a bottle of liniment, and marks, the money in our world.

8
00:00:28.312 --> 00:00:31.917
Let's open the knives and see what an item is made of.

9
00:00:32.367 --> 00:00:36.116
The description is what the narrator uses when the item shows up,

10
00:00:36.116 --> 00:00:39.751
so write it like the narrator would say it, not like a tooltip.

11
00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:41.300
Category and slot.

12
00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:43.562
Something you can equip needs a slot.

13
00:00:43.562 --> 00:00:49.186
Voyage's new worlds only come with armour slots, so I added one for weapons in the settings.

14
00:00:49.633 --> 00:00:55.098
Tier is how special it is, and estimated value is what one is worth in your money.

15
00:00:55.098 --> 00:00:58.097
The value has to fit inside the tier's range.

16
00:00:58.533 --> 00:01:01.045
Bonuses only count while it's equipped.

17
00:01:01.045 --> 00:01:06.132
Each point of damage adds ten percent, so the knives hit twenty percent harder.

18
00:01:06.132 --> 00:01:12.442
Each point of armour takes off a tenth of a percent, so the coat blocks five percent of every hit.

19
00:01:13.833 --> 00:01:16.158
There's no money number in Voyage.

20
00:01:16.158 --> 00:01:17.868
Your currency is an item.

21
00:01:17.868 --> 00:01:23.886
Name it in Item Settings, make an item with exactly that name, and it stacks like coins.

22
00:01:23.886 --> 00:01:25.049
Ours is the mark.

23
00:01:26.433 --> 00:01:28.411
Items, then Item Settings.

24
00:01:28.411 --> 00:01:31.681
Currency name is where you name your money.

25
00:01:32.133 --> 00:01:34.244
Tiers are the rarity ladder.

26
00:01:34.244 --> 00:01:37.636
Each one has a name, a colour, a value range,

27
00:01:37.636 --> 00:01:42.536
and how many bonuses the AI may give items it makes in that tier.

28
00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:46.870
Item slots are where gear can go when it's equipped: head, body,

29
00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:50.860
legs, feet and hands, plus the weapon slot I added for our knives.

30
00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:55.363
And starting items are given to every player, whatever they pick.

31
00:01:55.363 --> 00:01:59.464
Everyone in our show starts with five marks and a bottle of liniment.

32
00:02:00.867 --> 00:02:03.473
Items can boost attributes and skills too,

33
00:02:03.473 --> 00:02:08.128
but we haven't built those yet, so ours stick to damage and armour for now.

34
00:02:08.128 --> 00:02:09.493
We'll come back to it.

35
00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:14.369
That's items. Ours are linked in the description.

36
00:02:14.369 --> 00:02:20.316
Next time, attributes: the numbers behind every character, and what each one raises.

37
00:02:20.767 --> 00:02:24.715
I'm Dreamer. Now go build something weird, and I'll see you next time!

